#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:240
msgid "Enable Filter Attribute Image Swapping"
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:241
msgid "Showcase variation images based on applied filters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:242
msgid "On shop, category and tag pages, when a customer filters by an attribute value (for example <b>?filter_color=red</b> from the WooCommerce filter widget or block), the main product image changes to the <b>first image</b> of that value's <u>SVI Variations Gallery</u>.<br>If several values are filtered, the image is split into one part per value, using the layout set in \"Filter Attribute Split Layout Type\".<br>Products with no gallery for the filtered value keep their normal image. Only the first filtered attribute is used.<br><b>PRO:</b> galleries marked \"Hide from Product Loop\" are skipped, and the image can animate on hover."
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:254
msgid "Filter Attribute Split Layout Type"
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:255
msgid "Choose the layout style for displaying multiple variation images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:256
msgid "Select how multiple variation images should be displayed when a filter matches more than one variation on the Shop/Archive page. <b>Diagonal</b>: Images are split diagonally from bottom-left to top-right. <b>Vertical</b>: Images are stacked vertically. <b>Horizontal</b>: Images are arranged side by side horizontally. Default: Diagonal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:274
msgid "Enable Filter Attribute Animation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:275
msgid "Add sliding animation on hover"
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:277
msgid "When enabled, this option adds a sliding animation effect on hover for the Filter Attribute Split Layout (Diagonal, Vertical, Horizontal). The hovered image will expand, and the other images will slide to the remaining space."
msgstr ""

#: includes/library/wp-settings-framework/settings/svi-settings.php:278
